  "_about": "a common buzzard soaring in wide circles: broad, rounded wings held in a shallow V, the five fingered primaries spread, a short fanned tail finely barred; dark brown above, below the pale barred flight feathers with their dark trailing edge and the dark patch at the wrist, the pale band across the brown breast; a round head, the small hooked bill on its yellow cere, yellow feet drawn up (2026-11-08, review.py: claws) The claws RE-ROOTED (review.py): each a sheath as wide as the claw where it leaves the toe, sunk in it, the join faired (horn `fair`: grown out of the skin in its paint), darker at the base fading to its own colour at the point -- no pale cut edge where it leaves the fur.",
